Date: Sun, 2 Nov 2026 00:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] bridge: pace PinMAME with the host game clock

Pace the VPM emulation with the host-driven game clock each frame. The
time fence is otherwise set once at table init (core.vbs) and the libpinmame
game thread parks after ~10ms of emulated time: DMD freezes, switches never
process, solenoids never fire. Advancing the fence per step is exactly the
external synchronization the fence mechanism exists for (see time_fence
handling in cpuexec.c); the host owns the clock headless.

Target: vpinball/vpinball@64a480a96d1b972711fbb8eea014654c779b1e23

diff --git a/src/web/vpx_wasm_bridge.cpp b/src/web/vpx_wasm_bridge.cpp
--- a/src/web/vpx_wasm_bridge.cpp
+++ b/src/web/vpx_wasm_bridge.cpp
@@ -24,2 +24,3 @@ includes
 #include "utils/color.h"
+#include "pinmame/libpinmame.h"
 #include "parts/ball.h"
@@ -401,3 +401,6 @@ step
    if (!g_player)
       return;
+   // Pace PinMAME with the host-driven game clock: the VPM time fence is
+   // otherwise set once at table init and the emulation parks after ~10ms.
+   PinmameSetTimeFence(nowMs > 0.0 ? nowMs / 1000.0 : 0.001);
    g_player->StepHeadlessFrame(nowMs);
